  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **China** (1 review): The China Rider pairing is praised as an inspired way to open the second set [3]\n- **Rider** (1 review): Jeff's keyboard work stands out in Rider, rolling the song along with energy [3]\n- **Dew** (1 review): Mayer's second solo in Morning Dew is singled out as transcendent; Weir sings Morning Dew with strong, impassioned vocals [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **TLEO**: back after 102 archived shows (1073 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Sailor**: rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **Saint**: rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **China**: back after 103 archived shows (1075 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Rider**: back after 103 archived shows (1075 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **My Favorite Things**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Dew**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **UJB**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2019-06-01.cp4** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 170 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Recording is described as loud and uninterrupted, with the final crescendo coming through powerfully [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2019-06-01.cp4**: taped by doug kalley; transferred by doug kalley; source: nak cp4 (p48 jb mod)> tascam dr70d (busman mod) [1]",
